  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political landscape in Indonesia is currently focused on the selection of a new vice president following the vacancy left by Gibran. President Prabowo Subianto has provided a one-week timeframe for coalition parties to discuss and nominate candidates. The process requires that two names be formally presented to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) for consideration. Within the Gerindra Party, senior figures Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, Sugiono, and Ahmad Muzani have emerged as potential candidates, with party members emphasizing their familiarity with the president's political ideology. While various groups have expressed support for specific individuals, Sufmi Dasco Ahmad has publicly advised respect for the president's decision-making process. Concurrently, regional representative bodies have highlighted the necessity for any chosen candidate to effectively advocate for regional interests and local aspirations across the nation.",
